# Research content rules
- Inspect the existing content schema before editing paper metadata.
- Academic accuracy takes priority over marketing copy. Mark unfinished work as Work in progress and omit unpublished PDFs unless explicitly approved.
- Keep text in English. Each paper needs a precise question, a concise approach, and a transparent status.
- Do not fabricate findings or overstate causal identification.
- Ensure metadata fields match Zod schema and generated research pages link correctly.
